<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Ouroboros Aggregate Report ({{ n_runs }} runs)</title>
<style>
  body { font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; max-width: 1100px; margin: 2rem auto; color: #111; background: #f9f9f9; }
  h1 { font-size: 1.5rem; border-bottom: 2px solid #333; padding-bottom: .5rem; }
  h2 { font-size: 1.1rem; margin-top: 2rem; color: #333; border-left: 4px solid #4a90e2; padding-left: .6rem; }
  table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 1rem 0; background: #fff; }
  th { background: #4a90e2; color: #fff; padding: .4rem .7rem; text-align: left; font-size: .8rem; }
  td { padding: .35rem .7rem; font-size: .8rem; border-bottom: 1px solid #e0e0e0; }
  tr:hover td { background: #f0f4ff; }
  .meta-box { background: #fff; border: 1px solid #ddd; border-radius: 4px; padding: 1rem; font-size: .8rem; }
  .meta-box dt { font-weight: bold; float: left; clear: left; width: 180px; }
  .meta-box dd { margin-left: 190px; margin-bottom: .3rem; }
  .small-note { color: #666; font-size: .75rem; margin-top: .3rem; }
  .num { font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .stab-cell { display: inline-block; min-width: 2.2em; text-align: center; border-radius: 3px; padding: 1px 6px; color: #fff; font-size: .75rem; }
  .stab-1 { background: #2ecc71; }
  .stab-mid { background: #f39c12; }
  .stab-0 { background: #e74c3c; }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<h1>Ouroboros Aggregate Report</h1>
<div class="meta-box">
  <dl>
    <dt>Runs aggregated</dt><dd class="num">{{ n_runs }}</dd>
    <dt>Run IDs</dt>
    <dd>
      {% for rid in run_ids %}<div>{{ rid }}</div>{% endfor %}
    </dd>
  </dl>
</div>

<h2>Cross-Run ASR per Category</h2>
<table>
  <tr>
    <th>Category</th>
    <th>Runs</th>
    <th>Mean ASR</th>
    <th>Std (run-to-run)</th>
  </tr>
  {% for row in per_category %}
  <tr>
    <td>{{ row.category }}</td>
    <td class="num">{{ row.n_runs }}</td>
    <td class="num">{{ row.mean_asr }}</td>
    <td class="num">{{ row.std_asr }}</td>
  </tr>
  {% endfor %}
</table>
<div class="small-note">
  Std measures run-to-run variability. Near-zero std ⇒ the result is reproducible
  (model is consistently susceptible/resistant). Large std ⇒ outcomes depend
  heavily on the attacker's random sampling — consider more iterations or a
  different attacker temperature.
</div>

<h2>Per-Seed Stability</h2>
<div class="small-note" style="margin-bottom:.5rem;">
  Success rate across the {{ n_runs }} runs for each seed. Green = always
  succeeded, red = never succeeded; mid = inconsistent (the most interesting cases).
</div>
<table>
  <tr>
    <th>Seed ID</th>
    <th>Category</th>
    <th>Runs Present</th>
    <th>Success Rate</th>
    <th>Mean Iters to Success</th>
  </tr>
  {% for row in stability %}
  <tr>
    <td>{{ row.seed_id }}</td>
    <td>{{ row.category }}</td>
    <td class="num">{{ row.n_runs }}</td>
    <td>
      {% if row.success_rate == 1.0 %}
        <span class="stab-cell stab-1">{{ row.success_rate }}</span>
      {% elif row.success_rate == 0.0 %}
        <span class="stab-cell stab-0">{{ row.success_rate }}</span>
      {% else %}
        <span class="stab-cell stab-mid">{{ row.success_rate }}</span>
      {% endif %}
    </td>
    <td class="num">{{ row.mean_iters_to_success or "—" }}</td>
  </tr>
  {% endfor %}
</table>

<p style="font-size:.7rem; color:#888; margin-top:3rem;">
  Generated by Ouroboros v{{ version }} · {{ generated_at }}
</p>
</body>
</html>
